# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. Several gates read files line by line and
# fail on CRLF: the skill-discipline validator cannot find frontmatter, the
# dependency audit cannot find the lockfile's sections, and the generated
# agent-surface check reports every generated file as stale. A contributor on
# Windows with the common `core.autocrlf=true` therefore could not run
# `pnpm check` at all, while CI on Linux passed — the worst shape for a bug,
# because the person who hits it is the one least able to tell it is not their
# fault.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are never line-ending converted. `text=auto` already detects
# most of these; naming them is cheaper than discovering a corrupted font or
# sprite after it ships.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.parquet binary
